 "equipment_type": "VRF outdoor unit monitoring via BACnet gateway",
 "applies_to": "Daikin VRV outdoor units (mini-VRV, VRV-M, as grouped by CoolAutomation) read through a CoolAutomation gateway with PRO functionality.",
 "summary": "With PRO functionality, CoolAutomation gateways publish service data from each Daikin VRV outdoor unit over BACnet: ambient, suction, evaporating, condensing and discharge temperatures, EV openings, CT and inverter currents, fan step, compressor, heater and valve states, and protection-control flags such as retries and stepping-down or drooping control (55 objects for this series group). Monitoring only.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 64,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Instance = VA x 256 + index (object identifier bits 21-8 = VA, 7-0 = index). Points shown for VA 1; the guide does not explain how outdoor units receive their VA.",
  "Access set to read-only: these are measured service values, although the guide's type table lists PIV as read/write.",
  "Values marked (value x 0.1) or (value x 0.001) are raw and need scaling in the BMS.",
  "Object names are the guide's short names; descriptions are the guide's object descriptions.",
  "The guide repeats the description 'INV fin drooping cntl.' for the STD1/STD2 drooping-control objects; the short names show which compressor each belongs to."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Integration Guidelines - CoolMasterNet, CooLinkNet, CooLinkHub, CooLinkBridge",
  "doc_number": null,
  "revision_date": "Rev 0.5, 2019-04-29",
  "url": "https://coolautomation.com/Lib/doc/CoolMasterNet/manual/CoolMasterNet-BACnet-guidelines.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Use these objects to monitor Daikin outdoor equipment only; control stays on the CoolMasterNet indoor-unit objects. Map the outdoor block's VA and trend the key temperatures, compressor data and error state.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BI 276",
    "why": "Inverter compressor running",
    "name": "Comp1Inv"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 294",
    "why": "Defrost active",
    "name": "Dfrst"
   },
   {
    "ref": "IV 258",
    "why": "Ambient temperature, °C",
    "name": "AmbT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "IV 260",
    "why": "Evaporating temperature, °C",
    "name": "EvT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "IV 261",
    "why": "Condensing temperature, °C",
    "name": "CndT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "PIV 310",
    "why": "Inverter frequency, Hz",
    "name": "InvFrq"
   },
   {
    "ref": "PIV 274",
    "why": "Inverter current, A",
    "name": "InvCur"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 287",
    "why": "Unit error state",
    "name": "ErrState"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BACnet must be enabled on the gateway; these objects belong to its PRO (service data) functionality.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet MS/TP: activate on line L3 with 'line type L3 BAC' (L4-L7 also possible on CoolMasterNet); default frame 9600 8N1, change with 'line baud L3 <rate>_8N1'; MAC (TS) default 0x40 = 64, change with 'line myid L3 <hex>'. Reboot after each change.",
   "BACnet IP: enable with 'bacnet IP enable'; UDP port 47808 by default ('bacnet port <n>'). The server starts only once Ethernet is up with an IP address.",
   "Default device instance 64 (0x40); change with 'bacnet instance <n>'."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "The guide does not document how VAs are assigned to outdoor units; confirm instances with a BACnet discovery."
  ]
 },
